From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:44:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] libcameraservice: stop a HAL1 preview outside the
 client lock

CameraClient::stopPreview() called the HAL's stopPreview() with mLock
held. The Exynos HAL1 HAL (libexynoscamera, SM-T520) finishes a
picture that is still being taken before its stopPreview() returns: it
joins its picture thread. That thread's shutter and JPEG callbacks wait
for mLock in lockIfMessageWanted(), so closing the camera with a picture
pending hung for good.

Take a reference to the hardware and turn the preview callbacks off under
mLock, call stopPreview() without it, and take mLock again for the rest.
The provider serializes the call with the device's other calls, and a
disconnect in the meantime is caught by the mHardware check.

Test: camcycle on the SM-T520, 100 cycles including a close with a
picture pending per camera, no hang.

Change-Id: I73b9ad30797572e770bd1c8b9d08e3d76173aab8
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../libcameraservice/api1/CameraClient.cpp    | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/camera/libcameraservice/api1/CameraClient.cpp b/services/camera/libcameraservice/api1/CameraClient.cpp
index e196689a4f..fa8966e928 100644
--- a/services/camera/libcameraservice/api1/CameraClient.cpp
+++ b/services/camera/libcameraservice/api1/CameraClient.cpp
@@ -486,12 +486,23 @@ status_t CameraClient::startRecordingMode() {
 // stop preview mode
 void CameraClient::stopPreview() {
     LOG1("stopPreview (pid %d)", getCallingPid());
-    Mutex::Autolock lock(mLock);
-    if (checkPidAndHardware() != NO_ERROR) return;
+    sp<CameraHardwareInterface> hardware;
+    {
+        Mutex::Autolock lock(mLock);
+        if (checkPidAndHardware() != NO_ERROR) return;
 
+        disableMsgType(CAMERA_MSG_PREVIEW_FRAME);
+        hardware = mHardware;
+    }
 
-    disableMsgType(CAMERA_MSG_PREVIEW_FRAME);
-    mHardware->stopPreview();
+    // Not under mLock: a HAL may finish a picture that is still being taken before its
+    // stopPreview() returns (the Exynos HAL1 HAL joins its picture thread there), and the
+    // shutter and JPEG callbacks of that picture wait for mLock in lockIfMessageWanted().
+    // The provider serializes this call with the device's other calls.
+    hardware->stopPreview();
+
+    Mutex::Autolock lock(mLock);
+    if (mHardware == 0) return;  // disconnected meanwhile
     finishCameraStreamingOps();
     mPreviewBuffer.clear();
 }
